### The important discovery from comparing recreations

The “Blade Runner sound” is not actually one patch.

It is closer to this formula:

**CS-80 brass base + extreme aftertouch control + slow external ambience + human pitch movement**

The static patch is only about 40% of the sound.

The remaining 60%:

| Performance Element   | Importance          |
| --------------------- | ------------------- |
| Polyphonic aftertouch | Extremely high      |
| Ribbon controller     | Extremely high      |
| Manual filter opening | High                |
| Long reverb tail      | High                |
| Slight detuning       | Medium              |
| Oscillator waveform   | Medium              |
| Exact slider position | Lower than expected |

This is why people chasing the exact knob positions often fail: the CS-80 was designed as a **performance instrument**, not a preset machine. ([Arturia Forums][3])

